WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:01:15.000
A splash of fresh water will reach the depths of your heart. Those mighty blue waves can propel you forward or they can calm and soothe. Coast to Michigan coast. Simply feel the flow in the moment. And let those vast lakes, rivers and streams create everlasting memories. Jump right in and let fresh wash over you in Pure Michigan. Keep it fresh at Michigan.org. On the night of Friday, October 3, 2008, Canadian couple Trevor and Marissa were out walking their dog in the quiet suburban district of Mill Woods in Edmonton South.
一股清新的水流将触及你的心灵深处。那些蔚蓝的巨浪可以推动你向前，也可以安抚你的心。从密歇根州的一个海岸到另一个海岸。只需感受当下的水流。让那些广阔的湖泊、河流和溪流创造永恒的回忆。马上纵身跃入，让纯净的密歇根之水洗涤你。在 Michigan.org 保持新鲜感。2008年10月3日星期五晚上，一对加拿大夫妇特雷弗（Trevor）和玛丽莎（Marissa）正在埃德蒙顿南部米尔伍兹（Mill Woods）安静的住宅区遛狗。

2
00:01:15.000 --> 00:02:10.000
Suddenly, a young, dark-haired man staggered into their path from the direction of a nearby alleyway. He was hunched over, his shirt was torn, and he had a large welt on his sweaty face. He collapsed and rolled around in what the couple thought was an overly theatrical manner, then stood up and screamed, There's a guy attacking me, he's mugging me, please help me. He cried out, that's the guy, as a second hooded man wearing a black hockey mask with gold markings emerged from the alleyway. The man tapped his mask as though to adjust it, then slipped behind a fence. He peered over the top and called out to the injured man, come on Frank, come back. Though he sounded a lot harder than friendly, Trevor and Marissa felt uneasy.
突然，一个年轻、黑发的男子从附近一条小巷的方向踉跄着闯入他们的视线。他驼着背，衬衫撕破了，汗津津的脸上有一个大肿块。他倒地并打着滚，在夫妇俩看来，他的动作未免有些太戏剧化了，接着他站起身大喊：“有个家伙在袭击我，他在抢劫我，请帮帮我。”他大喊道：“就是那个家伙，”与此同时，第二个戴着带有金色斑纹的黑色曲棍球面具的连帽男子从巷子里走了出来。那名男子拍了拍面具，仿佛在调整它，然后溜到篱笆后面。他探出头朝受伤的男子喊道：“来吧，弗兰克，回来吧。”尽管他的语气听起来一点也不友好，但特雷弗和玛丽莎还是感到一阵不安。

3
00:02:10.000 --> 00:03:26.000
Suspecting this scenario was a setup to mug them, the couple hurried away as the dishevelled stranger cried out, Can you at least help me get to my car? Trevor wanted to help, but couldn't shake his suspicion that it was a trap. He and Marissa rushed home where they called the police. Officers were dispatched to the alleyway, but the two men were gone and nothing seemed out of the ordinary. They monitored the situation over the coming days, but received a note word from the alleged victim, or further sightings of the assailant in the hockey mask. 38-year-old Johnny Altinger lived alone in his small apartment in Edmonton,
这对夫妇怀疑这出戏是抢劫他们的圈套，于是匆忙走开，而那个衣衫褴褛的陌生人则大喊道：“你们至少能帮我走到我的车旁吗？”特雷弗想帮忙，但心中的怀疑挥之不去，总觉得这是一个陷阱。他和玛丽莎赶忙跑回家报了警。警察被派往那条小巷，但那两个男子已经不见了，一切看起来都很正常。他们在接下来的几天里密切关注着局势，但没有收到任何来自所谓受害者的消息，也没有人再次看到戴曲棍球面具的袭击者。38岁的强尼·阿尔廷格（Johnny Altinger）独自住在埃德蒙顿的一间小公寓里，

4
00:03:26.000 --> 00:04:22.000
where he was employed as a pipeline worker for oil-filled equipment manufacturer Argus Machine. His night shifts were spent in quality control, a job he neither loved nor hated, but which gave him satisfaction. Although they lived in different cities, he remained close with both his mother, Alfreda, and his older brother, Gary, and had a close-knit group of friends, some of whom stretched back to grade school. They described Johnny as good-natured, light-hearted, generous, thoughtful, quiet, and affectionate, with an optimistic outlook that he used to help others adopt a more positive attitude in their own lives. Johnny had a number of hobbies, but the two that drew most of his attention were motorbikes and computers. He owned two bikes, a Honda 500cc and a Yamaha 1200cc sport touring bike.
他在那里的油田设备制造商阿格斯机械公司（Argus Machine）担任管道工人。他的夜班工作是质量控制，这份工作他谈不上多喜欢，也谈不上讨厌，但它带给他一种满足感。尽管他们住在不同的城市，但他与母亲阿尔弗雷达（Alfreda）和哥哥加里（Gary）关系依然很近，并且有一群亲密无间的朋友，其中有些人甚至从小学起就认识了。他们将强尼描述为一个性格随和、乐观开朗、慷慨体贴、安静而深情的人，他总是带着乐观的心态，并用这种心态帮助其他人对生活采取更积极的态度。强尼有很多爱好，但最吸引他的两个是摩托车和电脑。他拥有两辆摩托车，一辆本田500cc和一辆雅马哈1200cc运动旅行摩托车。

5
00:04:22.000 --> 00:05:43.000
His free time was spent going on rides, playing paintball, dabbling in new-age spirituality, and enjoying the music of Elton John. At age 12, Johnny begged his mother to buy him a Commodore 64, an 8-bit home computer, sparking what would become a lifelong passion. From then on, he was an early adopter of computing tech, constantly upgrading his systems through the various hardware and software iterations. He was always willing to help out his less tech-savvy friends and family, with his brother Gary Ultinger stating, Countless times he would sacrifice his own responsibilities to rescue me by word-processing term papers, essays, and other important assignments while I was attending university. I owe much of my academic success to John. Johnny made many online friends who eventually became his friends in real life too, and by his 30s he was participating in online dating. He joined the two most popular free sites at the time, Plenty of Fish and Lava Life, and went on several dates of varying success, while remaining optimistic that he'd find his perfect match someday.
他的空闲时间都用来骑车、玩彩弹射击、涉足新时代灵性，以及欣赏埃尔顿·约翰（Elton John）的音乐。12岁时，强尼恳求母亲给他买一台康道尔64（Commodore 64）8位家用电脑，这激发了他终生的热情。从那时起，他便成了计算技术的早期使用者，通过各种硬件和软件的迭代不断升级他的系统。他总是乐于帮助那些对技术不太懂的朋友和家人，他的哥哥加里·阿尔廷格（Gary Ultinger）表示：“无数次，他为了帮我摆脱困境而牺牲自己的时间，帮我用文字处理机完成学期论文、散文和其他重要作业，当时我正在上大学。我的大部分学术成功都要归功于约翰。”强尼结交了许多网友，他们最终也成为了他现实生活中的朋友。到了30多岁时，他开始参与在线约会。他加入了当时最受欢迎的两个免费交友网站——Plenty of Fish和Lava Life，并约会了几次，结果各不相同，但他依然乐观地认为自己总有一天会找到真爱。

6
00:05:43.000 --> 00:06:55.000
On Plenty of Fish, Johnny connected with a 35-year-old woman named Jen, who sought fun times. Her profile pictures depicted an attractive woman in a bikini, although Johnny was aware that photos could be misleading. Banta between the pair indicated they were a good match, and they organised the date for the night of Friday, October 10, 2008. Jen didn't provide a street address for their meet-up, instead giving precise, turn-by-turn directions to a set location a 10-minute drive away from Johnny's apartment. She had written, Although this sounds exciting, I have to make sure you're not some kind of weirdo, and so far you seem to be fairly well put together, but anyone can lie online. Jen instructed Johnny to park in the driveway that looks like a forest, and sneak through a partially open garage door, making sure to press a button to close it behind him. She explained that a blanket would be spread out on the floor, as a friend was using the space as a workshop that weekend.
在 Plenty of Fish 上，强尼结识了一位35岁名叫简（Jen）的女子，她寻求的是有趣的时光。她的个人资料照片显示这是一个颇具吸引力的比基尼女郎，尽管强尼也知道照片可能会具有欺骗性。两人之间的网聊表明他们非常般配，于是他们将约会时间定在2008年10月10日星期五晚上。简没有提供见面地点的街道地址，而是给出了精确的、具体的路线指引，目的地是距离强尼公寓车程10分钟的一个地方。她写道：“虽然这听起来很刺激，但我必须确保你不是什么怪人，到目前为止你看起来还算靠谱，但网上的任何人都可以撒谎。”简指示强尼将车停在“看起来像森林”的车道上，然后悄悄穿过一扇半开的车库门，并务必按一下按钮将门在身后关上。她解释说，地板上会铺一条毯子，因为周末有朋友把这个空间当成车间使用。

7
00:06:55.000 --> 00:07:35.000
By following her directions, Jen would be able to see Johnny before letting him into the house. Quote, Maybe this is paranoid on my part, but I have to look after myself. My first instincts about people are never wrong, and I know to trust them. I want to play very much, but I have to be cautious, as I'm sure you can understand. If you're okay with this, let me know. If not, we'll have to miss each other. On a lighter note though, if we really get on, you said you had four days off. How long can I keep you for if I choose?
按照她的路线走，简就能在让强尼进屋之前先看到他。她说：“也许这算是我多疑，但我必须照顾好自己。我对人的第一直觉从来没有错，我知道应该相信它们。我非常想玩得开心，但我必须谨慎，我相信你能理解。如果你能接受这一点，请告诉我。如果不行，那我们就只能失之交臂了。不过轻松一点说，如果我们真的很合得来，你说你有四天假。如果我选择的话，我可以留你多久？”

8
00:07:35.000 --> 00:08:41.000
Maybe you should pack for a few days. Shortly before he left for his date, Johnny phoned his longtime trusted friend, Dale Smith. Dale thought the messages from Jen were suspicious, and joked that Johnny should call him once he got there to let him know he was safe. When Johnny arrived at the garage a short time later, he was met by a friendly and jovial man who explained he was using the location to direct films. He showed Johnny around the set where he was currently making a movie about a serial killer and let him hold a fake gun that was among various prop weapons on a metal table. The man told Johnny that Jen had been held up in traffic and didn't know what time she would be back. Disappointed, Johnny headed home and called Dale, recounting the failed date in his typical light-hearted manner. Shortly after Johnny hung up, Dale received an email message from his friend that read,
“也许你应该收拾好几天的行李。”在动身去约会之前不久，强尼给他的长期密友戴尔·史密斯（Dale Smith）打了电话。戴尔觉得来自简的信息很可疑，并开玩笑说强尼一到那里就应该给他打电话报平安。不久后，当强尼到达车库时，一位热情开朗的男子接待了他，该男子解释说他正在这里利用这个地点指导拍电影。他带强尼参观了目前正在拍摄一部关于连环杀手的电影的片场，并让强尼拿了一把金属桌上各种道具武器中的假枪。这名男子告诉强尼，简在路上堵车了，不知道几点才能回来。强尼感到很失望，于是回了家并给戴尔打电话，用他一贯轻松的语气讲述了这次失败的约会。强尼挂断电话后不久，戴尔收到了他朋友发来的一封电子邮件，上面写着：

9
00:08:41.000 --> 00:09:37.000
She's home now, I'm heading over again. Eager to hear the outcome of the date, Dale left numerous messages for Johnny on voicemail and text, but he didn't respond to any. Dale hoped that it had gone better than expected, and his friend just didn't have time to reply. By Sunday, his enthusiasm turned to concern when Johnny failed to meet for a scheduled motorbike lesson. Friends often quipped that Johnny was so reliable you could set your watch by him, and it was completely out of character for him to simply not show up without explanation. On Monday morning, Dale finally received an email from Johnny that read, I've met an extraordinary woman named Jen who was offered to take me on a nice long tropical vacation.
她现在到家了，我要再过去一趟。急切地想要知道约会结果的戴尔给强尼留了无数个语音和短信留言，但强尼都没有回复。戴尔希望约会进展得比预期还要顺利，而他的朋友只是没有时间回复。到了星期天，当强尼没有按计划去上摩托车课时，他的热情变成了担忧。朋友们经常开玩笑说强尼是个极守信用的人，甚至可以对照他的手表来调时，而他不作任何解释就无故爽约，这完全不符合他的性格。周一早上，戴尔终于收到强尼发来的一封电子邮件，上面写道：“我遇到了一位非凡的女性，名叫简，她主动提出带我去度一次美好的热带长假。”

10
00:09:37.000 --> 00:10:17.000
We'll be staying in her winter home in Costa Rica, phone number to follow soon. I won't be in town until December 10, but I will be checking my email periodically. Dale was stunned. Johnny would never skip work to take an impromptu holiday, and he didn't like warm destinations, once returning from a trip to Hawaii complaining of the heat. Dale knew if Johnny was truly leaving, it would take a few minutes to call, if only to ask Dale to store his beloved motorbikes. Furthermore, Johnny never signed off emails with his name,
我们将在她在哥斯达黎加的冬季度假屋里住一段时间，电话号码稍后会发给你。我直到12月10日才会回城，但我会定期查看电子邮件。戴尔惊呆了。强尼绝不会为了来一场说走就走的旅行而旷工，而且他不喜欢温暖的目的地，有一次从夏威夷旅行回来时还在抱怨天气太热。戴尔知道，如果强尼真的是要离开，至少会花几分钟打个电话，哪怕只是请戴尔帮忙照看他深爱的摩托车。此外，强尼在发邮件时从不用自己的名字落款，

11
00:10:17.000 --> 00:11:01.000
preferring to finish with a wisecrack about his friend. Believing Johnny did not author the message, Dale tested the sender by responding with a query, asking who would pick up Johnny's brother from the airport when he came to visit. Gary wasn't actually coming, and Johnny would know this, but Dale didn't get a reply. Other friends had also received the abrupt farewell email from Johnny, each replied asking him to get in touch, but none heard back. Like Dale, one was suspicious as to who had sent the email, as Johnny usually called her sunshine, and the message was missing his telltale signs,
而是喜欢用一句关于他朋友的俏皮话来结尾。戴尔坚信这条信息不是强尼写的，于是他用一个问题来测试发件人，询问当强尼的哥哥来探访时，谁会去机场接他。加里实际上并没有来，强尼也知道这一点，但戴尔没有收到回复。其他朋友也收到了强尼发来的这封语气生硬的告别邮件，每个人都回信让她保持联系，但没有一个人得到回复。和戴尔一样，其中一人对是谁发送了这封邮件心存怀疑，因为强尼通常叫她“阳光”，而且这信息里缺少他标志性的特征，

12
00:11:01.000 --> 00:11:48.000
including the joke or smiley face he ended their correspondence with. That same day, an update appeared on Johnny's Facebook page that read, Johnny is taking off to the Caribbean for a few months, see you all when I get back. His relationship status was also changed to, in a relationship. That evening, Johnny's boss received an email from him that read, Greetings, while I've certainly enjoyed my time at Argus, I have another offer that is just too good to pass up. So this is my notice that I will no longer be continuing my employment with your fine organization. I thank you for the opportunity, and rest assured, I would not be leaving
包括他用来结束通讯的笑话或笑脸符号。就在同一天，强尼的脸书（Facebook）主页上出现了一条更新，上面写着：“强尼要去加勒比海呆几个月了，等我回来再见大家。”他的感情状态也被改成了“恋爱中”。那天晚上，强尼的老板收到了他的一封电子邮件，上面写着：“问候，虽然我在阿格斯的工作确实很愉快，但我得到了另一个好到无法拒绝的offer。因此，在此通知各位，我将不再贵公司继续任职。感谢您给予的机会，请放心，我不会离开，”

13
00:11:48.000 --> 00:12:25.000
unless this new path I've chosen was truly life altering. Thank you, John Oltinger. There was no further contact from Johnny over the following days. His boss wrote back to him, John, there are many rumors floating around about what you have run off to do. All I need to know is where to forward your last check. Good luck in your endeavors, wherever they may be. Johnny ignored the message, and his $1,500 final paycheck went uncollected.
“除非我选择的新道路真的能改变我的一生。谢谢，约翰·阿尔廷格。”在接下来的几天里，强尼没有再与任何人联系。他的老板回信写道：“约翰，关于你到底跑去干什么，外面流言四起。我只需要知道把你的最后一张薪水支票寄到哪里。祝你在新的事业中一切顺利，无论你在哪里。”强尼忽略了这条信息，他那1500美元的最后薪水支票也无人领取。

14
00:12:25.000 --> 00:13:00.000
Meanwhile, his MSN messenger status changed too, I've got a one-way ticket to heaven, and I'm never coming back. And his Facebook page was updated once more to say, Johnny's wondering why anyone would leave son and surf to come home to snow and stress. Carrie Lynn Sousa was the wife of one of Johnny's friends. Although she had never met him, she decided to reach out to Johnny over Facebook in an effort to assist his friends. In a private message, she wrote,
与此同时，他的MSN聊天状态也变了：“我买了一张通往天堂的单程票，再也不会回来了。”他的脸书主页再次更新，写道：“强尼想知道为什么有人会离开阳光与冲浪，回到冰雪和压力交织的家中。”凯莉·林恩·苏萨（Carrie Lynn Sousa）是强尼的一位朋友的妻子。尽管她从未见过他，但她决定通过脸书联系强尼，以协助他的朋友们。她在一条私信中写道：

15
00:13:00.000 --> 00:13:32.000
Hi John, please respond as soon as you get this, or at least call Dale. Everyone is concerned for you. Thanks, Carrie Lynn. Surprisingly, she received a prompt reply that read, No need to be worried, I'm on vacation and loving it. The internet is much easier to use than phones due to terrible reception and cost. I just need to get away for a while, and I'm with someone wonderful. I'll try to get in touch with Dale as soon as possible,
“嗨，约翰，请一看到就回复，或者至少给戴尔打个电话。大家都为你担心。谢谢，凯莉·林恩。”令她惊讶的是，她很快收到了回复，上面写着：“无需担心，我在度假，过得很开心。由于信号太差且费用高昂，互联网比电话好用得多。我只是需要离开一段时间，而且我和一个很棒的人在一起。我会尽快尝试与戴尔取得联系，”

16
00:13:32.000 --> 00:14:20.000
but in the meantime, let him know I'm having the time of my life. Carrie Lynn provided Johnny with a call collect phone number he could reach Dale on, and told him to ring by 6.30pm, or they would be following up with Edmonton City Police. When the call never came, the police were alerted, but they weren't overly concerned. They accepted Johnny's explanation that he had gone on holiday with a woman he had met online. Unconvinced, Johnny's friends decided to break into his apartment to search for clues. They arrived at Johnny's four-story condo, where his motorcycle sat uncovered in the outdoor parking lot of the complex. His red Mazda 323 was missing.
“但在那之前，请告诉他我正过着我一生中最快乐的时光。”凯莉·林恩给强尼提供了一个对方付费电话号码，他可以通过这个号码联系到戴尔，并告诉他必须在晚上6:30之前打电话，否则他们将报警。当电话始终没打来时，人们报警了，但警方并没有表现出过分担忧。他们接受了强尼的解释，即他和在网上认识的一个女人去度假了。强尼的朋友们并不买账，决定破门进入他的公寓寻找线索。他们来到了强尼所在的四层公寓楼，他的摩托车没有盖车衣，就停在小区的露天停车场里。他的红色马自达323不见了。

17
00:14:20.000 --> 00:15:14.000
They broke a window to gain access to Johnny's apartment, finding dirty dishes in the sink, a paintball gun resting on his unmade bed, an open CD case on the white leather couch in the lounge room. His motorcycle jacket hung over the back of a kitchen chair and his helmet on the table. The mess itself wasn't unusual, as Johnny was known to tidy up when he expected guests. Yet, the overall state of the apartment did not correlate with a person who had gone on holiday for an extended period of time. Johnny's laptop was missing, and strangely, so was his printer. In a surprise discovery, a desk drawer contained his passport, confirming he could not have gone to Costa Rica. The group returned to the Edmonton Police with the evidence they had gathered.
他们砸碎了一扇窗户以进入强尼的公寓，发现水槽里有脏盘子，一张彩弹枪放在他没有整理的床上，客厅的白色皮沙发上放着一个打开的CD盒。他的摩托车夹克挂在一把厨房椅子的靠背上，头盔放在桌子上。房间乱糟糟的这倒并不罕见，因为大家都知道强尼在预料有客人来时才会收拾房间。然而，公寓的整体状况与一个离家去外地度长假的人完全不符。强尼的笔记本电脑不见了，奇怪的是，他的打印机也不见了。令人意外的是，他们在一个抽屉里发现了他的护照，这证实他根本不可能去过哥斯达黎加。这群人带着收集到的证据回到了埃德蒙顿警察局。

18
00:15:14.000 --> 00:16:16.000
Realizing the circumstances of his alleged departure didn't add up, police opened a missing persons file for Johnny Ultinger on Friday, October 17, 2008, one week after his last confirmed communications. A search for his car at the airport came up dry, and his name was absent from the passenger lists of all departing international flights. The detailed instructions Jen emailed Johnny for their first date provided the strongest lead. Detective Bill Clark was surprised to learn that Johnny had forwarded the instructions to two friends before going out, including Dale Smith, who recalled his friend saying something like, If anything happens to me, you'll know where to look. There were constant warnings to women on dating sites to exercise caution and to let someone know where they were going, but it was far less common for men to do so.
意识到他所谓的离职和离开的种种情况根本对不上号，警方于2008年10月17日星期五——即他最后一次被确认与外界联系的一周后——为强尼·阿尔廷格立案失踪人员档案。警方在机场搜寻他的汽车一无所获，所有离境国际航班的乘客名单中也没有他的名字。简在电子邮件中发给强尼的关于他们第一次约会的详细路线指引成了最强有力的线索。比尔·克拉克（Bill Clark）侦探惊讶地得知，强尼在出门前将这些路线指引转发给了两个朋友，其中包括戴尔·史密斯，戴尔回忆起他的朋友曾说过类似这样的话：“如果我出了什么事，你知道去哪儿找。” dating网站上经常对女性发出警告，提醒她们保持警惕并让别人知道她们要去哪里，但男性这样做则要少得多。

19
00:16:16.000 --> 00:17:15.000
The directions led detectives to a garage in a laneway in the residential area of Mill Woods in the city's southeast. They arrived close to midnight, finding the building locked with a combination padlock. The windows were covered up, but one constable peaked through a small hole and could see a light on inside. There didn't appear to be anyone in there, and the interior was clean. They knocked on the door to their joining house, but there was no answer. An application for a search warrant was denied, as there was no evidence a crime had been committed. However, police inquiries led to Kirkside Real Estate, who confirmed the garage had been leased to Mark Twitchell, an independent filmmaker. On the evening of Saturday, October 18, police called Mark and told him there was a problem with the garage he was renting.
这些路线将侦探们引向了该市东南部米尔伍兹住宅区一条巷子里的一个车库。他们接近午夜时分抵达，发现大楼被一把密码挂锁锁上了。窗户被遮挡住了，但一名警员透过一个小孔往里看，可以看到里面亮着灯。里面似乎没有人，而且内部很干净。他们敲了敲与其相连的房子的门，但无人应答。搜查令的申请被拒绝了，因为没有证据表明发生了犯罪行为。然而，警方的调查锁定了科克斯ide房地产公司（Kirkside Real Estate），该公司证实该车库已经租给了独立电影制作人马克·特维特切尔（Mark Twitchell）。10月18日星期六晚上，警方打电话给马克，告诉他他租的车库出了点问题。

20
00:17:15.000 --> 00:18:12.000
The director readily agreed to come and open it up. At around 11.30pm, a maroon-coloured Pontiac Grand AM sedan pulled up outside the garage and Mark Twitchell emerged. He was agitated as he had to pull over twice while on his way over to answer calls from Kirkside Real Estate, from which he surmised that someone had been using the garage without his knowledge and left the lights on. As Mark went to let the police into the building, he expressed surprise at the padlock on the door, explaining it was different from the one he'd been using. His combination padlock was silver on the outside with a black plastic dial in the centre, but this one was pure metal. Mark said he didn't know the combination and allowed officers to break it off.
这位导演爽快地答应过来打开它。晚上11点半左右，一辆褐红色的庞蒂亚克大阿姆（Pontiac Grand AM）轿车停在车库外，马克·特维特切尔从车里走了出来。他显得有些心神不宁，因为在赶来接听科克斯ide房地产公司电话的路上，他不得不把车停下两次，他由此推测有人在不知情的情况下使用了车库并把灯开着了。当马克去给警察开门时，他对外面的挂锁表现出惊讶，解释说这与他一直使用的锁不同。他的密码挂锁外面是银色的，中间有一个黑色的塑料拨盘，但这把锁是纯金属的。马克说他不知道密码，并允许警员将其砸断。

21
00:18:12.000 --> 00:19:06.000
Mark explained that he rented the garage for $175 a month. The residential space was rented to temporary foreign workers while someone else lived in the basement. Mark didn't have any contact with the other people in the building. As they entered the garage, a strong smell lingered inside indicating something had recently been burned in there. The odor emanated from an oil drum in one corner that had scorch marks and contained charred remains. Mark said he ordered the barrel to use as a garbage can and it had not been scorched when he had last seen it. He also noted that several things were out of place. Most of his roll of duct tape had been used, all his garbage bags were gone and an unopened bottle of cleaner was now half empty.
马克解释说，他以每月175美元的价格租下了这个车库。住宅区租给了临时外国劳工，而地下室则住着另一个人。马克与大楼里的其他人没有任何接触。当他们进入车库时，里面弥漫着一股浓烈的气味，表明不久前里面有什么东西被烧过。这股气味散发自角落里的一个油桶，桶上有烧焦的痕迹，里面装着烧焦的残骸。马克说他订购这个桶是打算当垃圾桶用的，他上次看到它时并没有被烧焦。他还注意到有几样东西摆放得不对劲。他的一大卷强力胶带大部分都用完了，所有的垃圾袋都不见了，一瓶未开封的清洁剂现在也用了一半。

22
00:19:06.000 --> 00:20:14.000
All the windows were covered from the inside and when the roller doors were closed it was impossible to see in. Mark explained that in late September he had filmed a scene for his short psychological thriller about a serial killer titled House of Cards. As it occurred at night time, he had to block out the daylight that poured into the building. There were a few red spatters about the garage, which Mark clarified were remnants of fake blood. The attending officers decided to call their staff sergeant and while waiting, Mark Twitchell chatted with Constable Christopher Maxwell in a police car preparing his written statement. There was a pleasant conversation, mostly centred on Mark's billmaking and interest in the Star Wars movie franchise. When asked if he would be willing to come back to the station to answer some questions, Mark agreed. It was around 3.30am when Detective Mike Tabla interviewed Mark Twitchell.
所有的窗户都从内部被遮挡起来了，当卷帘门关上时，里面什么也看。马克解释说，在9月下旬，他为他的微型心理惊悚片《纸牌屋》（House of Cards）拍摄了一个场景，片名暂定为《纸牌屋》。由于故事发生在夜间，他必须挡住射入大楼的日光。车库里有一些红色的血迹斑点，马克澄清说那是假血的残留物。出警的警员决定呼叫他们的值班中士，在等待期间，马克·特维特切尔坐在警车里与克里斯托弗·麦克斯韦（Christopher Maxwell）警员闲聊，同时准备他的书面供词。这是一次愉快的谈话，主要围绕马克的电影制作以及他对《星球大战》电影系列的兴趣展开。当被问及是否愿意回警局回答一些问题时，马克爽快地答应了。大约凌晨3点30分，迈克·塔布拉（Mike Tabla）侦探对马克·特维特切尔进行了讯问。

23
00:20:14.000 --> 00:21:25.000
He was forthcoming and helpful, though seemed more interested in talking about his film career. He shared how he'd lined up A-list actors and the co-producer who worked on the 2001 Heist film Ocean's 11 for an upcoming comedy and discussed his plans to submit House of Cards to festivals or pitch it to investors in the hopes they would fund a feature-length version or television series. He described the scene in the garage, detailing how the production crew had made large quantities of fake blood using corn syrup and food dye, creating a realistic but messy result. Detective Tabla pointed out the coincidence that Mark was filming a serial killer movie in the very place a man had disappeared from. Mark agreed, stating, I got this weird chill because it just doesn't sit right, so the first thing I start asking myself is, who knows about what we do there and what our schedule looks like. Mark provided a list of people who had worked on House of Cards and others who had accessed the garage.
他态度坦率、乐于助人，尽管他似乎对谈论自己的电影生涯更感兴趣。他分享了他是如何请到一线演员以及曾参与2001年劫案电影《十一罗汉》（Ocean's 11）的联合制片人来制作一部即将上映的喜剧，并讨论了他计划将《纸牌屋》送去电影节参展，或者向投资者推销以期获得资金来拍摄长片版或电视剧的计划。他描述了车库里的那个场景，详细讲述了制作团队如何用玉米糖浆和食用色素制作大量的假血，从而创造出逼真但凌乱的效果。塔布拉侦探指出，马克在一个男子失踪的地方拍摄一部连环杀人电影，这未免太巧合了。马克表示赞同，并说道：“我感到一阵莫名的寒意，因为这感觉太不对劲了，所以我脑子里首先浮现的问题是，谁知道我们在那里做什么以及我们的拍摄日程是什么样的？”马克提供了一份曾参与《纸牌屋》制作的人员名单以及其他可以进入该车库的人员名单。

24
00:21:25.000 --> 00:22:52.000
He said the last time he had been there was Friday, October 10, the day Johnny Altinger's friends last confirmed contact with the missing man. When asked if he knew of someone called Johnny Altinger, Mark was certain he had never heard the name. The detective provided details about Johnny's last known activity and how he had gone to the garage to meet Jen, but instead encountered a man working on a film. Mark appeared baffled, claiming not to know anybody by the name of Jen. A rudimentary background check revealed that Mark Twitchell came from a good home and had no history of violence or criminality, although there was an old bankruptcy that would soon be discharged. After the lengthy interview, Mark was released with instructions to contact police if he recalled anything that may assist in their search for Johnny Altinger. The next day, Detective Tabla received a three-page email from Mark Twitchell, in which he recalled several strange occurrences he believed might be related to their investigation. Weeks earlier, Mark's car was broken into while he was at a show with a friend named Joss, who had worked odd production jobs on House of Cards and designed the film's website.
他说他最后一次去那里是在10月10日星期五，也就是强尼·阿尔廷格的朋友们最后一次确认与这位失踪男子取得联系的日子。当被问及是否认识一个叫强尼·阿尔廷格的人时，马克坚称他从未听过这个名字。侦探向他提供了强尼最后已知的活动细节，以及他是如何去车库见简，却遇到一个在拍电影的人的经过。马克显得十分困惑，坚称不认识任何叫简的人。初步背景调查显示，马克·特维特切尔出身于一个良好的家庭，没有暴力或犯罪前科，不过他有一宗即将解除的旧破产记录。经过漫长的讯问后，马克被释放，并被指示如果想起任何可能协助搜寻强尼·阿尔廷格的事情，请与警方联系。第二天，塔布拉侦探收到了一封来自马克·特维特切尔的三页电子邮件，他在邮件中回忆了几件他认为可能与他们的调查有关的奇异事件。几周前，马克和一位名叫乔斯（Joss）的朋友去看演出时，马克的车被砸了。乔斯曾在《纸牌屋》中做过零散的制作工作，并设计了该片的网站。

25
00:22:52.000 --> 00:24:10.000
The offender stole Mark's sunglasses, the loose cash kept in the cup holder, and a bunch of receipts. One was for financial services company Western Union and featured Mark's residential address, while two others related to the garage and listed its address. Then, on the night of Sunday, October 12, Mark returned home after visiting his in-laws to find the front door to his home unlocked. He didn't notice anything missing or any signs of an intruder and chalked it up to paranoia and fatigue. On Wednesday, October 15, Mark had just driven to a petrol station to fill up a jerry can and had pulled over to answer a call when a stranger tapped on his window. The Caucasian man was around 6 feet 2 inches tall, medium-built, with black mid-length hair. Mark rolled down his window and the man asked if he'd like to buy his car, a red Mazda 323, as he was set to receive a brand new BMW from a sugar mama he had hooked up with. The man wanted to get rid of his Mazda before taking off on an all-expenses paid vacation and offered to sell it to Mark for whatever cash he had on him.
罪犯偷走了马克的太阳镜、放在杯架里的零钱以及一叠收据。其中一张是金融服务公司西联汇款（Western Union）的，上面有马克的住宅地址，另外两张与车库有关，上面列出了车库的地址。接着，在10月12日星期日晚上，马克拜访完岳父母家回到家里，发现前门没有锁。他没有发现任何东西丢失或有入侵的迹象，便把这归咎于多疑和疲劳。10月15日星期三，马克刚刚开车去加油站给一个汽油桶加油，随后把车停在路边接电话，这时一个陌生人敲了他的车窗。这个白人男子身高约6英尺2英寸（约1.88米），中等身材，留着黑色中长发。马克摇下车窗，那男子问他是否想买他的车——一辆红色的马自达323，因为他准备从一个包养他的富婆那里拿到一辆崭新的宝马。这男子想在踏上一场费用全包的假期前把他的马自达脱手，并提出只要马克身上有多少现金就把车卖给他。

26
00:24:10.000 --> 00:25:05.000
Mark replied that he only had $40 and was surprised when the man accepted the small payment. Although suspicious, Mark permitted the man to follow him to the garage. He described in the email to Detective Tabla, quote, He's even killed disposition all but disappeared when we got to the garage and I was getting a weird vibe from him. The man was obviously keen to get going, handing Mark the Mazda's keys, registration and insurance before taking off. Mark quickly realized the car had a manual transmission, which he didn't know how to operate, and had his friend Joss collect the Mazda and store it. Mark finished up his email, writing, I don't mind saying this is all seriously stressing me out.
马克回答说他身上只有40美元，当那名男子接受了这么少的一笔钱时，他感到很惊讶。尽管心存疑虑，马克还是允许那名男子跟着他开车去车库。他在给塔布拉侦探的电子邮件中描述道：“当我们到达车库时，那种他杀的迹象几乎消失了，我从他身上感觉到了一种诡异的气息。”这名男子显然急着离开，把马自达的钥匙、行驶证和保险单交给了马克，然后就匆忙离开了。马克很快意识到这辆车是手动挡的，而他根本不会开手动挡，于是他让他的朋友乔斯把马自达开走并存放起来。马克在电子邮件的结尾写道：“我不介意直说，这一切真的让我压力山大。”

27
00:25:05.000 --> 00:25:59.000
Identity theft is the first concern. My home being compromised is now another one, and we're strongly considering getting an active security system installed next week. I feel violated and angry that anyone was ruining around in my personal stuff without my knowledge, and now I'm greatly worried that they likely know where I live. My car has a distinctive appearance and an easily identifiable custom plate, and I'm wondering if this fellow who pawned the car off on me had seen mine before and might have been waiting for me or following me. I just don't know anymore. He could have been the person who broke into my car as well. There's a hundred different scenarios rushing through my head right now, and I'm not a fan of any of them. Detective Tabla shared Mark's email with his colleagues.
身份盗窃是首要担忧。我的家遭到侵入现在成了另一个担忧，我们正在认真考虑下周安装一个活跃的安全系统。有人在不知情的情况下把我的个人物品翻了个底朝天，这让我感到被侵犯和愤怒，现在我非常担心他们很可能知道我住在哪里。我的车外观独特且有容易识别的个性化车牌，我在想，这个把车死乞白赖推销给我的家伙是不是以前见过我的车，可能一直在等我或跟踪我。我真的不知道该怎么办了。他也可能是那个砸了我车的人。现在有一百种不同的剧本在我脑海里飞驰，而我一个也不喜欢。塔布拉侦探将马克的电子邮件分享给了同事们。

28
00:25:59.000 --> 00:26:55.000
The odd stories only served to heighten their suspicions and take a closer look at the director. 29-year-old Mark Twitchell lived with his wife, Joss, and their eight-month-old daughter in a home they had purchased the previous year. Joss had insisted on the move as shared loathe to their previous neighborhood and threatened that their marriage might not last should they remain there. Mark got a mortgage to secure a new split-level home with a white picket fence in the Riverside District of St. Albert. Joss was Mark's second wife. The couple had met through an online dating service and married in 2006. By 2008, their relationship was strained and they were sleeping in separate bedrooms. Joss was unhappy about Mark's filmmaking efforts, which took up a large amount of his time for little financial gain.
这些离奇的故事非但没有打消疑虑，反而加剧了他们的怀疑，让他们决定更仔细地审视这位导演。29岁的马克·特维特切尔与妻子乔斯（Joss）以及他们八个月大的女儿住在他们前一年购买的房子里。乔斯坚持要搬家，因为他们都极度厌恶之前的社区，并威胁说如果继续呆在那里，他们的婚姻可能就维持不下去了。马克申请了房贷，在圣阿尔伯特（St. Albert）的河畔区（Riverside District）买下了一栋带白色栅栏的新错层住宅。乔斯是马克的第二任妻子。两人通过网络交友服务相识，并于2006年结婚。到2008年时，他们的关系已经很紧张，开始分房睡了。乔斯对马克的电影制作工作很不满，因为这占据了他大量的时间，却几乎没有什么经济回报。

29
00:26:55.000 --> 00:28:02.000
It was part of Mark's identity. He was a regular cosplayer dressing up in costumes as Wolverine, Predator, and nearly every major Star Wars character while attending sci-fi and fantasy conventions where he took photos with the stars of his favorite series. One particularly elaborate costume of the Transformer Bumblebee won him over $3,000 in prizes for Radio Halloween Contests. He later sold it for a substantial amount. But his obsession came at the expense of his family, so Joss insisted they start attending couples therapy. Mark also agreed to weekly one-on-one sessions with a psychiatrist, and it seemed as though they were working. Despite their problems, Mark regarded Joss as a wonderful mother to their daughter, whom he believed was exceptionally adorable. On Monday, October 20, Mark Twitchell visited the Edmonton Police Service headquarters for a second interview.
这是马克身份的一部分。他是一个狂热的影视服装扮演者（Cosplayer），在参加科幻和奇幻大会时，会打扮成金刚狼、铁血战士以及几乎所有主要的《星球大战》角色，并在会上与他最喜欢的系列的明星合照。其中一套特别精致的“变形金刚大黄蜂”服装为他赢得了超过3000美元的广播万圣节比赛奖金。他后来以很高的价格把它卖掉了。但这种痴迷是以牺牲他的家庭为代价的，因此乔斯坚持他们开始进行夫妻心理治疗。马克还同意每周与精神病医生进行一次一对一的会谈，情况似乎有所改善。尽管存在种种问题，马克仍然认为乔斯是一个伟大的母亲，对他们的女儿疼爱有加，他觉得女儿异常可爱。10月20日星期天，马克·特维特切尔第二次前往埃德蒙顿警察局总部接受讯问。

30
00:28:02.000 --> 00:29:06.000
It was performed by the forces star interrogator Bill Clark, known as the Pip Bull, a 30-year veteran detective skilled in the old-school style of grilling suspects. Mark acknowledged his legal right to have a lawyer present, but deemed it unnecessary. Every facet of Mark's story was probed, including his encounter with the unknown man who sold him a Mazda 323 for $40. He recalled the seller had a Celtic knot tattooed on his neck about three inches in diameter. The Mazda was later located in the possession of Mark's friend and crew member Joss, and confirmed to be Johnny Ultinger's vehicle. Detective Clark switched gear and changed his line of questioning, narrowing his focus on Johnny Ultinger. He pressed Mark, asking him questions like, What do you think happened? Do you think somebody has done something to harm him? Do you think he's really missing?
这次审讯由该局的王牌审讯专家比尔·克拉克（Bill Clark）主持，他被称为“斗牛犬”，是一位拥有30年经验的侦探，擅长老派的严厉盘问风格。马克承认了自己有权请律师在场的法律权利，但他认为没有必要。马克故事中的每一个方面都受到了盘问，包括他遇到那个以40美元向他出售马自达323的陌生男子的遭遇。他回忆说，那个卖家脖子上有一个直径约三英寸的凯尔特结纹身。这辆马自达后来在马克的朋克兼剧组人员乔斯那里被找到，并被证实确实是强尼·阿尔廷格的座驾。克拉克侦探转换了方向，改变了审讯路线，将焦点缩小到强尼·阿尔廷格身上。他向马克施压，问他诸如以下的问题：“你认为发生了什么？你认为有人做了什么伤害他的事吗？你觉得他是真的失踪了吗？”

31
00:29:06.000 --> 00:30:06.000
Mark's response to which was that he didn't know. When asked, How do you think the results of this investigation are going to come out on you? He replied, Well, positively, I would think. I've been trying to tell you guys everything that I know. The bombardment of questions continued, leading into the possibility Johnny had met with foul play and Mark's opinions of the person who would carry out such a crime. Mark believed the perpetrator should go to prison with no mercy. When asked point blank if he had any involvement in Johnny's disappearance, Mark responded, No. Detective Clark continued to apply pressure, but Mark remained firm. After a short break at the interrogation's two and a half hour point, Detective Clark explicitly accused Mark of being involved,
